meta {
  name: Close All Linked Thread Tickets
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/requests/{{requestId}}/close
  body: multipart-form
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  note: Resolved for the whole thread — all linked requests handled together.
  closeThread: true
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const tc = res.body.threadClose || { closed: [], skipped: [] };
    console.log("⏳ Closed #" + res.body.id, "| Status:", res.body.assignedStatus);
    console.log("🔗 Linked tickets closed:", tc.closed.map(r => r.id));
    if (tc.skipped.length) console.log("⚠️ Skipped:", tc.skipped);
  } else if (res.status === 403) {
    console.log("❌ Not authorized to close this ticket");
  } else if (res.status === 409) {
    console.log("❌ This ticket is already closed or pending acknowledgement");
  } else {
    console.log("❌", res.body.error);
  }
}

docs {
  # Close All Linked Thread Tickets

  Same endpoint as **02-Requests → Close Ticket**, with `closeThread=true`.
  Used by the "Close all linked thread tickets" button in the web app.

  ## What it does
  1. Closes `{{requestId}}` exactly like a normal close (→ "Pending Acknowledgement").
  2. Finds the thread (root + all replies) and closes every other **open** ticket in it
     with the same resolution note and attachments (files are uploaded once and shared).
  3. Already-closed / pending-acknowledgement tickets are left alone.
  4. Tickets the caller isn't authorized to close are **skipped**, not failed.

  ## Body (multipart-form)
  | Field       | Type   | Description                              |
  |-------------|--------|------------------------------------------|
  | note        | string | Resolution note (used for every ticket)  |
  | files       | File   | Optional attachments, up to 10           |
  | closeThread | "true" | Close all linked tickets too             |

  ## Response
  The closed request, plus:
  ```json
  "threadClose": {
    "closed":  [ { "id": 101, "assignedStatus": "Pending Acknowledgement", ... } ],
    "skipped": [ { "id": 102, "reason": "Not authorized" } ]
  }
  ```

  ## Errors (for `{{requestId}}` itself)
  - **403** — not authorized to close it
  - **404** — request not found
  - **409** — already closed or pending acknowledgement
}
